[E0303] Error: cannot apply `+` to `i64` and `u64`
    ╭─[ err/537_what_does_not_widen/main.wip:18:15 ]
    │
 18 │     val c = a + b
    │             ┬ ┬ ┬
    │             ╰────── `i64`
    │               │ │
    │               ╰──── operands of different types
    │                 │
    │                 ╰── `u64`
    │
    │ Note: an integer is taken as a wider type that holds every value of it, and neither of these holds the other; `as` converts one, keeping the low bits of a value that does not fit
────╯
